1. Rust dependencies embedded in the published binaries
-------------------------------------------------------

The `rumoca` and `rumoca-lsp` binaries published to GitHub Releases are
statically linked and therefore embed the code of every crate in their
dependency graph. Their licenses, and the full text of each, are in

    THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md

generated by infra/licenses/generate.sh from infra/licenses/about.toml. Every
license there is permissive except `option-ext` (MPL-2.0, reached through
`dirs` -> `dirs-sys`); THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md carries the source-availability
notice that MPL-2.0 section 3.2 requires. No dependency of a published binary
is under a copyleft-only license.

The Zenoh ecosystem is `EPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0`; Apache-2.0 is selected, so no
copyleft term applies. It is optional in `rumoca-sim` but `transport-zenoh` is a
default feature of the `rumoca` binary crate, so it is in the shipped binary and
is attributed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md. A build that enables features outside
the default set should regenerate that file for its own feature set.


